WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.660
Send someone an HTML file, and they get a download.

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:07.124
Send a Markdrop link, and they get the page.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.137
Here's how files work on Markdrop.

00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:14.877
Drop a file on the upload page.

00:00:15.571 --> 00:00:21.431
The preview is drawn in your browser before anything uploads, and the title and link come from the file name.

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:27.269
An HTML page runs, scripts and all.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.640
It's served from a separate domain, in a sandbox, so it can't touch your Markdrop account, or your readers'.

00:00:35.971 --> 00:00:37.531
A PDF opens as pages.

00:00:38.427 --> 00:00:41.607
A workbook opens as a grid, with a tab for each sheet.

00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:48.388
A Word document becomes clean text, and a zipped site opens at its index page, with its links working.

00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:53.459
Screen recordings up to two gigabytes play in place.

00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:57.371
They stream, and they seek, without downloading the whole file.

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:01.379
Spot a mistake after you've shared it?

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:02.319
Replace the file.

00:01:03.207 --> 00:01:08.487
The link, who can open it, and its views stay the same, and open pages switch to the new version.

00:01:10.925 --> 00:01:15.065
Markdrop keeps the last five versions, so you can bring an earlier one back.

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:17.412
Old versions are never public.

00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:24.734
Upload your first file, with a free account, at markdrop.in/upload.
